# =============================================================================
# Docker build-context exclusions for the two root images, Dockerfile.api and
# Dockerfile.web, both built from the repository root.
#
# The satellite image is NOT built from here: it has its own Dockerfile and
# .dockerignore under satellite-ml/, and deploy/40-satellite-job.sh builds it
# with satellite-ml/ as the context. That whole tree is therefore excluded
# below — neither root image reads a byte of it.
#
# Strategy: exclude-list. Everything not listed here is shipped to the daemon,
# so newly added source directories work without touching this file.
# Keep this in sync with .gcloudignore.
# =============================================================================

# --- VCS / editor / OS -------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
*.swp

# Claude Code worktrees hold a FULL second copy of the repo — never ship it.
.claude

# --- Node / Next.js ----------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules is reinstalled from package-lock.json inside the image, and
# .next / out are rebuilt. Shipping them makes the context ~10x larger and can
# poison the build with host-arch native modules.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
out
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
.venv
**/.venv
venv
**/venv
# ml-service/agrotech is a checked-out virtualenv (agrotech/lib/python3.14/...),
# NOT the Python package. The package lives in ml-service/src/agrotech_ml.
ml-service/agrotech
ml-service/catboost_info

# --- Runtime state that must never be baked into an image --------------------
# ml-service/artifacts holds ~170 MB of trained .joblib models on a developer's
# machine, and has been a symlink to /tmp on some checkouts. Either way it must
# not enter the context: models are distributed via AGROTECH_MODELS_GCS_URI and
# downloaded at startup. To bake them into the image instead, put the
# .joblib/.json files in deploy/models/ (see that directory).
ml-service/artifacts
# User uploads (may contain personal data) and local SQLite databases.
ml-service/uploads
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# The satellite module builds from its own context (satellite-ml/Dockerfile with
# satellite-ml/.dockerignore), so none of it belongs in the api/web context.
satellite-ml

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Never bake credentials into a layer. Secrets arrive at runtime from Secret
# Manager. Docker matches .dockerignore patterns against the FULL relative path,
# so a bare `.env` would only cover the repo root — `**/` is required to also
# catch ml-service/.env, which exists on dev machines and holds a real API key.
# (.env.example files are deliberately kept — they are documentation.)
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*-service-account*.json
**/*-sa-key*.json
**/credentials.json

# --- Infra / docs that no image needs ----------------------------------------
docs
deploy/terraform
deploy/*.sh
deploy/*.py
deploy/lib
deploy/models/README.md
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.*.yml
README.md
